		{"id":"exegesis","type":"text","text":"## Scripture · Galatians 1–6\nSix sessions, one chapter per gathering (DEC-076). Each chapter divides into Part 1 and Part 2.\n\nApply the Complexity Gate: how deep to go while keeping the pace.","x":30,"y":70,"width":560,"height":360,"color":"#4A90D9"},
		{"id":"synthesis","type":"text","text":"## Theology · source priority\nScripture governs. Keller’s Galatians For You is the primary course-development and question resource.\n\nPeterson’s Traveling Light is secondary, especially for freedom.\n\nRecord actual edition/page contributions; common research supports both packages.","x":710,"y":70,"width":560,"height":360,"color":"#9B72CF"},
		{"id":"formation","type":"text","text":"## Formation · separate goals\nDevelop Men’s and Women’s particular discipleship focuses, grounded in the text and actual pastoral context.\n\nBelonging · Beholding · Becoming\n\nSpecific goals are not supplied yet; do not fill them from assumptions. See the two audience lanes below.","x":1390,"y":70,"width":560,"height":360,"color":"#65A86B"},
		{"id":"design","type":"text","text":"## Gathering Flow · approved by Russ (DEC-076)\n6:30–6:50 check-in\n6:50–7:20 Part 1: 20 exegesis + 10 discussion\n7:20–7:50 Part 2: 20 exegesis + 10 discussion\n7:50–8:00 regroup: final thoughts, prayer requests, pray out\n\nFollows S.O.A.P.: Scripture → Observation → Application → Prayer. Breakout tables optional.","x":2070,"y":70,"width":560,"height":340,"color":"#D6B34B"},
		{"id":"discussion","type":"text","text":"## Discussion · Keller question source\nGather actual questions from Galatians For You. Record edition/page, direct use/adaptation, question intent, and leader follow-up.\n\nSelect and adapt separately for Men’s/Women’s formation goals and each 10-minute discussion block.","x":2070,"y":440,"width":560,"height":310,"color":"#D96B6B"},
		{"id":"production","type":"text","text":"## Resource Output · separate packages\nPaul develops dated Men’s and Women’s two-page handouts (Weekly Recap format), teaching notes, and slides when needed.\n\nHandout: Last Session Review · Scripture (Bibles open) · Part 1 · Part 2 · Reflections and Close Prayer.\nRuss, Miranda, and Conner lead with these materials.","x":2750,"y":70,"width":560,"height":360,"color":"#9098A1"},
		{"id":"source-notes","type":"text","text":"## Source / calendar details\nActual Keller question excerpts/notes and edition/pages\nPeterson freedom notes and references\nNotion links/versions · Bible translation\n\nDifferent dates for Men’s/Women’s packages. Holiday adjustments and dated study calendar remain open.","x":30,"y":710,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"#4A90D9"},
		{"id":"next","type":"text","text":"## Next action · Paul\nRead chapter 1 with Keller as primary and Peterson secondary. Develop distinct formation goals and dated two-block resource packages for the two Collectives.\n\nConfirm next study dates/resource deadlines.","x":2070,"y":800,"width":560,"height":250,"color":"#D6B34B"},
		{"id":"session-template","type":"file","file":"Groups Ministry/10 Templates/Records/Curriculum Session.md","x":1390,"y":480,"width":560,"height":180,"color":"#9098A1"},
		{"id":"master-link","type":"text","text":"## Link two phase 03 gathering masters\nAfter Paul confirms synthesis/goals/outline, create separate Men’s/Women’s masters in 03 Develop Content.\n\nActual dates/goals; shared research linked. Keep this project brief/Canvas in phase 02.","x":1390,"y":720,"width":560,"height":310,"color":"#65A86B"},
		{"id":"review","type":"text","text":"## Review and release handoffs\nPaul confirms phase 02 direction and reviews actual phase 03 editable content.\n\nResource Producer verifies actual exports. Paul’s final review precedes phase 04 library promotion. Record actual response/date/version here in the project brief.","x":2750,"y":480,"width":560,"height":310,"color":"#9098A1"},
